  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Focused on the stolen car, Elena discovers her car is missing and threatens Barinov, who then forces a confession from Fedya. Let's listen closely to Chef Barinov and Elena's exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Постучаться не учили?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я звоню в полицию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Где моя машина?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятия не имею.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Значит так, мне все это надоело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Если через пять минут...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "моей машины не будет на месте...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "я заявляю об угоне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Вы меня хорошо поняли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Все.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Перед тем, как я тебя убью...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "ответь мне на вопрос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты зачем увез машину?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, у него не получилось приехать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Он сказал, чтобы я машину привез.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как ты ее вообще завел?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Ну, чем открыл, тем и завел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты зеркало починил?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around The Stolen Car line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Постучаться не учили?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Didn't they teach you to knock?' Chef Barinov turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'to knock', followed by 'taught'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я звоню в полицию.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am calling the police.' Elena chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'call' for the ongoing action, followed by 'the police'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Где моя машина?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where is my car?' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'where' directly with 'a car' to make the point directly in conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Понятия не имею.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have no idea.' Chef Barinov expresses this naturally by combining the word for 'concept' with 'have'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Значит так, мне все это надоело.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is it. I have had enough.' Elena puts the word for 'then' together with 'has got boring' in a crisp, natural spoken turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Если через пять минут...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If in five minutes...' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be' here, linking 'five' directly with 'minutes' to make the point directly in conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "моей машины не будет на месте...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My car is not back...' The phrasing opens with 'cars' before bringing in 'will be' and 'place' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "я заявляю об угоне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am reporting it stolen.' Elena chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'to declare' for the ongoing action, followed by 'theft'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Вы меня хорошо поняли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you understand me?' Elena turns a statement into a question purely through rising intonation on the word meaning 'good', followed by 'did you understand?'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Все.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is all.' Elena delivers a punchy conversational reaction built around the Russian word meaning 'all'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Перед тем, как я тебя убью...",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Before I kill you...' The phrasing opens with 'how' before bringing in 'I'll kill' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "ответь мне на вопрос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Answer one question.' Chef Barinov leads with the direct command form meaning 'answer', followed by 'question'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты зачем увез машину?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why did you take the car?' Chef Barinov puts the word for 'what for' together with 'to take away' and 'car' in a crisp, natural spoken turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Шеф, у него не получилось приехать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Boss, he could not make it.' Fedya uses the perfective verb meaning 'worked out' to focus on the single completed result, pairing it with 'to come'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
